            <ArticleTitle>Blood flow in the microvasculature of the conjunctiva of man.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>995-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cinephotomicrography of capillary blood flow in conjunctival vessels of man were carried out at 116 pictures per second. Red cells did not move in streamlines but rather in a heterogenous mixing type of flow. Flow in vessels of patients whose red cells were grossly aggregated was very slow and often stagnant.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
